(ARG-03 — `arguments's name` is the program name, argv[0].
 The raw value is the path the binary was invoked by, so printing it
 would make this probe unre-runnable; it printed `./p` when run by hand
 with the command below. What IS deterministic is that it is the same
 string as argument 0, so the probe asserts that identity instead.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-03.vox -o p && ./p alpha
 Args: alpha
 expected output:
   the name is argument zero
   the name is present
)
a text called 'the program name' is arguments's name.
a number called nothingth is 0.
a text called 'argument zero' is the argument at the nothingth.
If 'the program name' is 'argument zero' then,
    Print "the name is argument zero".
Otherwise,
    Print "the name differs from argument zero".

If 'the program name' is empty then,
    Print "the name is empty".
Otherwise,
    Print "the name is present".
